==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|doubtlesse}}, {{l|en|doutless}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|douteles}}, {{m|enm|dowteles}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|doubt|less}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdaʊ̯tləs/}}
* {{a|Canada}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdʌʊ̯tləs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-doubtless.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Characterized by or experiencing no [[doubt]] at all, [[certain]]; [[undoubted]]; [[undoubting]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1880|author=B. Stewart; P. G. Tait|title=The Unseen Universe|publisher=Macmillan|location=London|page=xiii
|passage=There are those who have '''doubtless''' faith in revelation.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1927|author=[[w:Edgar_Rice_Burroughs|Edgar Rice Burroughs]]|title=The Outlaw of Torn|chapter=7|passage=It is '''doubtless''' that the old reprobate who sued for his daughter's hand heard some unsavory truths from the man.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Free from fear or suspicion.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King John|IV|i|passage=Pretty child, sleep '''doubtless''' and secure.}}

