===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# Without doubt; [[certainly]]; [[definitely]]; very [[probably]], [[in all likelihood]]; [[doubtlessly]].
#: {{syn|en|indubitably|undoubtably|undoubtedly|unquestionably|without a doubt|without doubt|indisputably|''see also'' [[probably#Synonyms|probably § Synonyms]]}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XXXIX|61|{{...}} And, '''doubtless''', unto thee is given<br>⁠A life that bears immortal fruit<br>⁠In such great offices as suit<br>The full-grown energies of heaven.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1893|author=[[w:Ambrose_Bierce|Ambrose Bierce]]|title=The Realm Of The Unreal
|passage=I cannot remember that I spoke a word, though '''doubtless''' I did.}}
#* {{RQ:Baum Wizard of Oz|page=21|passage=The men, Dorothy thought, were about as old as Uncle Henry, for two of them had beards. But the little woman was '''doubtless''' much older: her face was covered with wrinkles, her hair was nearly white, and she walked rather stiffly.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1920|author=w:Edward Carpenter|title=Pagan and Christian Creeds|year_published=1921|location=New York|publisher=Harcourt, Brace and Co.|page=9|passage=There is also in these matters of Science (though many scientific men would '''doubtless''' deny this) a great deal of "Fashion".}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian |date=June 26, 2017 |author=w:Alexis Petridis |title=Glastonbury 2017 verdict: Radiohead, Foo Fighters, Lorde, Stormzy and more |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170626070544/https://www.theguardian.com/music/2017/jun/26/glastonbury-2017-verdict-radiohead-foo-fighters-lorde-stormzy-and-more |passage=Thom Yorke’s onstage pronouncements became less abstract and more effusive, they played the songs the less committed audience members '''doubtless''' wanted to hear in the first place: Paranoid Android, Creep, Fake Plastic Trees and Karma Police. At the end of the latter, Yorke happily led an audience singalong.}}

